  "track.ux.lab.curve.title": "Problem discovery curve",
  "track.ux.lab.curve.intro": "found(n) = 1 − (1 − L)^n, where L is the share of problems one participant uncovers. Default L = 31% (Nielsen, \"averaged across many projects\") — an assumption you can change. [[src:nn-5users]] [[badge:quant-model]]",
  "track.ux.lab.curve.L": "L (share found by one user)",
  "track.ux.lab.curve.n": "n (participants)",
  "track.ux.lab.curve.read": "With n = {n}, L = {L}: the model predicts {f} of the problems found.",
  "track.ux.lab.curve.desc": "A curve of the share of problems found against the number of participants.",
  "track.ux.lab.curve.compare": "By the formula itself, 1 round × 15 users ({one}) and 3 rounds × 5 users ({three}) give nearly the same coverage. The benefit of several small rounds lies where the formula is silent: fixing between rounds, checking the fixes, and uncovering problems that were masked (Nielsen advises splitting the budget into several rounds).",
  "track.ux.lab.curve.assume": "Assumptions: similar users using the product in similar ways; independent problems with a uniform L. Rare problems need more users; distinct user groups need separate tests; quantitative questions need ≥ 20 users. [[src:nn-howmany]]",
